msgctxt "Item:40575:0:9"
msgid "Tentacle Thresher"
msgstr "Акула-октопожор"

#. ja: ベッコウダンゴウオ
#. de: gepanzert[a] Lumpfisch
#. fr: lompe de Bekko
#. column 2: bekko rockhuggers
#. column 8: The round body of this wavekin allows it to be carried swiftly through the ocean's currents, which might explain why it clings so desperately to the ocean's rocks.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Bekko Rockhugger
msgctxt "Item:40576:0:0"
msgid "bekko rockhugger"
msgstr "бекко-скалолаз"

#. de: gepanzert[a] Lumpfische
#. fr: lompes de Bekko
#. column 0: bekko rockhugger
#. column 8: The round body of this wavekin allows it to be carried swiftly through the ocean's currents, which might explain why it clings so desperately to the ocean's rocks.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Bekko Rockhugger
msgctxt "Item:40576:0:2"
msgid "bekko rockhuggers"
msgstr "бекко-скалолазы"

#. ja: 丸い魚体で活発に動くオサードランプサッカーの仲間<br>紅玉海沖合の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G2に設定可能]
#. de: Ein Freund des othardischen Lumpfisches, bekannt für seinen runden Körper und ruckartigen Bewegungen. Seltener Fisch der Rubinsee. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe M ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un poisson tout rond vivant caché dans les roches. Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois dans la Mer de Rubis.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de taille moyenne]
#. column 0: bekko rockhugger
#. column 2: bekko rockhuggers
#. column 9: Bekko Rockhugger
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:40576:0:8"
msgid "The round body of this wavekin allows it to be carried swiftly through the ocean's currents, which might explain why it clings so desperately to the ocean's rocks.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]"
msgstr "Круглое тело позволяет этой рыбке быстро носиться в морских течениях. Может, поэтому она так отчаянно цепляется за скалы.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для рыбного отпечатка среднего размера.]"

#. ja: ベッコウダンゴウオ
#. de: Gepanzerter Lumpfisch
#. fr: Lompe de Bekko
#. column 0: bekko rockhugger
#. column 2: bekko rockhuggers
